<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">assist</ansi>

The assist command attacks whatever a party member is
currently fighting. It is a quick way to join combat
alongside your allies without having to identify the
target yourself.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">assist</ansi>             Attack your party leader's target.
  <ansi fg="command">assist [name]</ansi>      Attack a specific party member's target.

If you are the party leader, <ansi fg="command">assist</ansi> with no argument
will target whatever the first fighting party member is
engaged with.

<ansi fg="yellow">Requirements:</ansi>
  - Must be in a party
  - The party member must be in the same room
  - The party member must be in combat

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help attack</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help party</ansi>
